{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/AlecKriebel/Math/pulls/259","id":4703398579,"node_id":"PR_kwDOTfIvP88AAAABGFgqsw","html_url":"https://github.com/AlecKriebel/Math/pull/259","diff_url":"https://github.com/AlecKriebel/Math/pull/259.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/AlecKriebel/Math/pull/259.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/AlecKriebel/Math/issues/259","number":259,"state":"open","locked":false,"title":"5100026: reviewed k407 outer focal-antipedal vertex-centroid invariant","user":{"login":"AlecKriebel","id":6109370,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYxMDkzNzA=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/6109370?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/AlecKriebel","html_url":"https://github.com/AlecKriebel","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AlecKriebel/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AlecKriebel/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AlecKriebel/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AlecKriebel/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AlecKriebel/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AlecKriebel/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AlecKriebel/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AlecKriebel/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AlecKriebel/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"## Result\nProposed status: **claimed_solved, 1/5 substantive author turns**.\n\nFor every primitive even-period elliptic billiard with a strict confocal elliptical caustic, the vertex centroid of the outer polygon's antipedal with respect to either original billiard focus is phase-independent. Primitive stars are included. All real antipedal intersections are finite, and the N=4 case is treated directly. This is the arithmetic vertex centroid C0, with no signed-area denominator.\n\n## Independent review\nThe unchanged full proof received a separate adversarial AI review: **PASS_COMPLETE_SOURCE_TARGET**. The complete review, exact controls and separate high-precision diagnostics are included. This is an unrefereed draft, with classical inputs credited and no historical-novelty certification.\n\n- [Full proof](https://github.com/AlecKriebel/Math/blob/math/5100026-k407-wip/unsolved_math_prioritization/attempts/5100026/PROOF.md)\n- [Independent review](https://github.com/AlecKriebel/Math/blob/math/5100026-k407-wip/unsolved_math_prioritization/attempts/5100026/independent_review/INDEPENDENT_REVIEW.md)\n- [Publication status and scope](https://github.com/AlecKriebel/Math/blob/math/5100026-k407-wip/unsolved_math_prioritization/attempts/5100026/PUBLICATION_STATUS.md)\n\nThe author freeze is preserved. A narrow bibliographic correction distinguishes arXiv v11 *Eighty New Invariants* from the final companion *Fifty New Invariants*; table identity and mathematics are unchanged. Only this problem's QUEUE.md row is modified. No source PDFs, private material, release or DOI is included.","created_at":"2026-10-01T12:07:07Z","updated_at":"2026-10-01T12:07:07Z","closed_at":null,"merged_at":null,"merge_commit_sha":"81a882cc744e6b43f1bd588f7498bda0de525414","assignees":[],"requested_reviewers":[],"requested_teams":[],"labels":[],"milestone":null,"draft":true,"commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/AlecKriebel/Math/pulls/259/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/AlecKriebel/Math/pulls/259/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/AlecKriebel/Math/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/AlecKriebel/Math/issues/259/comments","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/AlecKriebel/Math/statuses/0524ed734ee8185681d030af98088259134a6af7","head":{"label":"AlecKriebel:math/5100026-k407-wip","ref":"math/5100026-k407-wip","sha":"0524ed734ee8185681d030af98088259134a6af7","user":{"login":"AlecKriebel","id":6109370,"node_id":"M